# RC000 Implementation Gate

**Authority:** [`docs/rc/RC000-clearstrata-constitution.md`](docs/rc/RC000-clearstrata-constitution.md) (RC000)

RC000 is a constitutional document. **Never modify RC000** unless the user explicitly instructs a constitutional amendment.

RC000 has **higher priority** than any future RC (RC009, RC010, RC011, …), feature specs, and convenience refactors.

Coexists with [`docs/00_ClearStrata_Constitution.md`](docs/00_ClearStrata_Constitution.md) (FD-001). On conflict between implementation choices, **RC000 CDGL layer rules win for RC feature work**.

## Mandatory preflight (before any RC implementation code)

1. **Read RC000** — [`docs/rc/RC000-clearstrata-constitution.md`](docs/rc/RC000-clearstrata-constitution.md)
2. **Identify the CDGL layer** — Issue · Governance · Meeting · Voting · Execution · Accountability · Continuous Improvement
3. **Explain loop impact** — state whether the change **strengthens** the Democratic Governance Loop (traceability, participation, accountability, memory)
4. **Stop on conflict** — if the design violates RC000 (especially Principles 1–4), **do not write code**; explain the conflict and propose a compliant design first

## Milestone gate (RC000 Appendix A — MGS)

Before implementing **any milestone** (M1, M2, M3…):

1. Verify the milestone document in `docs/milestones/` complies with [**RC000 Appendix A (MGS)**](docs/rc/RC000-clearstrata-constitution.md#appendix-a--milestone-governance-standard-mgs) (Principles A1–A10).
2. If **no milestone document exists**, **request architectural documentation** before implementation — do not proceed with code.

Guidance (non-authoritative): [`docs/architecture/Milestone-Governance-Standard.md`](docs/architecture/Milestone-Governance-Standard.md)

## CGDP gate (RC000 Appendix B)

Before implementation, **verify CGDP compliance** — [`docs/architecture/CGDP-ClearStrata-Governance-Documentation-Pyramid.md`](docs/architecture/CGDP-ClearStrata-Governance-Documentation-Pyramid.md)

Reason top-down: **FD → RC000 → GDR → ADR → RC → Milestone → Implementation**

If a proposal attempts to **redefine a higher documentation layer**, **stop implementation** and explain the constitutional conflict.

Examples: RC redefining ADR · ADR redefining GDR · Implementation skipping Milestone or RC

## Non‑negotiable layer boundaries

| Layer | Must | Must not |
|---|---|---|
| **Governance** | Matter, discussion, evidence, AI analysis | Author formal resolutions |
| **Meeting** | Author/edit/delete/reorder resolutions until snapshot freeze | Replace voting or execution |
| **Voting** | Approve/reject frozen resolutions | Edit resolution text or threshold |
| **Execution / Accountability** | Tasks, owners, review | Bypass meeting + vote |

## RC000 red flags (stop and explain)

- Copying Matter title/body into a formal resolution in Governance
- Editing resolution content after snapshot freeze
- Voting UI or RPCs that mutate resolution wording
- New parallel resolution objects that bypass Meeting
- Modules that skip Governance → Meeting → Voting for binding decisions

## When this gate applies

Any task labeled RC*, governance/meeting/voting/execution work, or architecture that touches CDGL layers — including investigations that recommend implementation.
